    "name": "AI Incident Intelligence API",
    "description": "Ready-to-run collection for the AI Incident Intelligence backend (Phases 1-4).\n\n## How to use\n1. Start the app: `mvn spring-boot:run` (default `baseUrl` is `http://localhost:8080`).\n2. Import this file into Postman (Import -> File).\n3. Run the collection **top-to-bottom** with the Collection Runner - tokens and ids are captured automatically by test scripts, so every request works in sequence.\n4. Emails are randomized per run (`alice_169...@example.com`), so the collection is re-runnable against a populated database.\n\n## What is covered\n- Registration for CUSTOMER / AGENT / ADMIN, duplicate-email rejection\n- Login, wrong-password 401, JWT access + refresh tokens\n- Refresh token rotation and replay rejection (401)\n- Incident CRUD, validation errors (400), pagination + filtering\n- Status lifecycle (OPEN -> IN_PROGRESS -> RESOLVED) and illegal transitions\n- Security matrix: no token 401, invalid token 401, cross-customer access 403, role violations 403\n- ADMIN user management",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
